Package: ivate
Title: Sensitivity Analysis for the ATE with Instrumental Variables
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("First", "Last", email = "you@example.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides tools for sensitivity analysis and partial identification
    of the average treatment effect (ATE) in instrumental variable (IV)
    settings. Under the standard IV assumptions of Angrist, Imbens, and Rubin
    (1996), point identification of the ATE is precluded by two unobserved
    quantities: the mean potential outcome under control for always-takers
    and the mean potential outcome under treatment for never-takers. This
    package derives the thresholds on these sensitivity parameters at which
    the ATE equals a policy-relevant decision threshold, and computes bounds
    on the ATE under user-supplied assumptions. Both one-sided and two-sided
    non-compliance are handled automatically.
